{{template "advance_preamble" .}}

Create feature test plan for {{.id}}: "{{.title}}".

CHECK COMPLEXITY TIER: Read feature metadata via {{template "get_json" .}} | jq -r '.metadata.complexity_tier'.

READ:
(1) Parent epic UAT acceptance plan for acceptance scenarios this feature must satisfy
(2) Feature PRD at {{.file_path}}/prd.md for requirements and acceptance criteria
(3) Feature architecture docs (02-08 series) for API contracts, data models, and integration points
(4) Triage or research report for codebase patterns and existing test infrastructure
(5) Sibling feature test plans for cross-feature test coordination

SCALE OUTPUT BY TIER:
- SIMPLE (lightweight test plan: AC test matrix only -- concrete test cases for each acceptance criterion with inputs/expected outputs/edge cases, reference existing test patterns, 1-2 pages)
- STANDARD (focused test plan: AC test matrix, API contract test cases if applicable, component test strategy for key components, integration scenarios for cross-feature touchpoints, 3-5 pages)
- COMPLEX (comprehensive test plan per quality skill: all 6 sections -- epic UAT scenario decomposition, component test strategy, API contract test cases, integration scenarios, AC test matrix, performance/security approach)

Tests must trace to USER GOALS and persona needs.

CALLER-PATH CONTRACT (MANDATORY for STANDARD and COMPLEX; required for SIMPLE if test exercises a service with a production caller above it):
Every test case must declare (per quality/workflows/test-planning.md Step 5.8):
- Production entrypoint (function + argument shape production callers actually use)
- Lowest allowed mock seam
- Forbidden mocks (seams that hid prior bugs — e.g. helper-test signatures that production never passes, factory wirings that must not be bypassed)
- Counter-factual (one sentence: what a buggy impl would do that this test would catch)
Internal-only opt-out is permitted only for pure value objects / private functions with no production caller above them in the diff, with a written one-line justification.

EXIT GATE varies by tier:
- SIMPLE (every AC has test case, actionable for TDD; caller-path contract present where applicable)
- STANDARD (AC coverage, API contracts tested, integration points identified, every test case has caller-path contract)
- COMPLEX (full 6-section plan, epic UAT traceability, quality skill checklist passes including Step 5.8 caller-path contracts and Step 7.5 codex red-team)

Write to 09-test-plan.md.
